module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_running_unit_masked_loses_its_drop_ins_at_the_next_reload

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyImpossible }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_running_unit_masked_loses_its_drop_ins_at_the_next_reload: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_running_unit_masked_loses_its_drop_ins_at_the_next_reload" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyImpossible, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "no built route constructs a mask of an active unit: every mask route reads the unit's systemd state and dispatches systemctl mask only on a proven-stopped unit. Sufficient for: no route the corpus builds reaches a running unit with a mask, so its drop-ins survive the next daemon-reload. The shared drain actuator's MaskWhileRunning admission arm is the sole remaining constructor that masks without that check and is built by no production route, so retiring that arm makes mask-of-an-active-unit unconstructible." } },
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a systemd unit that is still RUNNING is masked. `systemctl mask` reloads the manager, and a unit whose file is masked (-> /dev/null) loads none of its drop-ins, so at that reload, and at any later one, the live unit loses every property its drop-ins carried: the runner slot's memory caps (template drop-ins on srv1, per-slot system.control set-property drop-ins on srv4) and its Slice=. Its processes leave system-actions\\x2drunner.slice for a cgroup with no memory.max on its path.",
    "HARM: a required v2-bootstrap job on such a slot runs with no memory envelope; the envelope gate refuses it (MemoryEnvelopeAbsent at start, MemoryReceiptUnreadable when its unit's memory.events vanished mid-job), so the required check goes red on main and on every PR whose job lands there. Fail-closed, no wrong answer, but merges stall repo-wide.",
    "RECEIPT 2026-11-04, srv4, fleet-converge run 41861708547 (runner_host_file_converge at main 08d2cc56, gunbc#15819's slot-tree fold): the fold drained every out-of-date slot through drain_and_mask_runner_slot_over, which masks a busy unit and leaves it running (DrainWaitForJob). Twelve busy slots were masked at 16:22Z; witnesses runs 41861662327 and 41865951805 on main and 41866118627 on gunbc#15618 refused on srv4-01/02/08/12/15. Reported by quick-newt-573, loyal-deer-449 and silent-bee-845; loyal-deer-449 restored the units by unmask and restart.",
    "THE FALSE PREMISE IT RESTED ON, stated in gunbc.runner.runner_slot_actuation before this row: 'The mask comes first and is safe at any time: it only stops the unit being started again.' Masking is safe only on an inactive unit.",
    "REPAIR (slot-tree fold): gunbc.runner.runner_slot_actuation SlotDrainAdmission NeverMaskARunningUnit, used by gunbc.runner.runner_host_file_converge converge_runner_slot_tree: an idle unit is stopped BEFORE it is masked, and a busy or stopping unit gets no leg at all and stays pending, unmasked, for a later run. Witness: test.claim.runner.runner_slot_actuation_witness never_mask_a_running_unit_leaves_a_busy_slot_untouched_and_stops_an_idle_one_before_masking.",
    "REPAIR (cap bracket, node fleet-cap-bracket-keeps-running-units, 2026-11-15): the bracket's mask primitive gunbc.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket mask_slot_only_over no longer masks unconditionally. It reads the unit and dispatches systemctl mask only when the unit is proven stopped (slot_state_stopped: Inactive or Failed); a unit that is active, activating, reloading or deactivating is left unmasked (none). The bracket has NO stop leg, so unlike DrainSteps in the shared actuator it cannot stop-then-mask a unit whose job finished mid-wait; the only safe mask is on a proven-stopped unit, exactly runner_slot_actuation's NeverMaskARunningUnit. The old premise 'the mask inhibits successors and is safe at any time' was this class's invalid state held for the length of the wait. A running unit now stays pending and unmasked and the bracket withholds the cap write fail-closed for a later pass. RED-on-main / GREEN-after control: test.claim.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket_witness a_cap_bracket_pass_never_masks_a_running_runner_unit -- a bracket pass over a fixture host with a systemd-active runner unit issues no mask for it, while a proven-stopped owned unit is still masked (so the control cannot pass vacuously).",
    "OPEN, SAME CLASS, NOT REPAIRED HERE: runner_slot_actuation's default slot_drain_plan (admission MaskWhileRunning) and drain_runner_slot_under_over (reached via drain_and_mask_runner_slot_over) still close admission on a running unit. No production route constructs them, but they remain the model's only remaining way to mask a live unit. The trigger is retiring the MaskWhileRunning admission arm so no built route constructs a mask of an active unit. Nothing on these routes contains the harm (a masked-while-running unit's drop-ins are simply lost at the next daemon-reload), which is why the rung is read below the ladder rather than Mitigatable. These routes are outside node fleet-cap-bracket-keeps-running-units and are filed as a follow-up node.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
